> On Fri, Jul 07, 2006 at 10:34:04PM +0700, Yanis Batura wrote:
>> B: na cumki .i ro prenu zo'u gonai terspe panzi gi nalterspe panzi

> You have to leave out the {zo'u} here, or you'd have to write {ro da poi prenu
> zo'u da co'e}

{ro prenu zo'u ...} is perfectly grammatical, and I don't see any reasons why adhere to strict logics in everyday speech.
{ro broda zo'u brode} is a natural reduction of longer {ro da poi broda zo'u da brode}.

mi'e .ianis.

